false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-702a-b6a0-ce17875e667d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-796c-8b3c-aa437bd658ff","question":"Which of these quotes is from the film \'On the Waterfront\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Terry Malloy says the line to his brother Charlie in a taxi, recalling how he was steered away from a promising boxing career.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-7cd8-bb12-51c6e9e1f360","description":"\"You don\'t understand! I coulda had class. I coulda been a contender. I could\'ve been somebody, instead of a bum, which is what I am.\"","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-7927-9b88-b2de399297fd","description":"\"You\u2019re going to go through life thinking that girls don\u2019t like you because you\u2019re a nerd. And I want you to know, from the bottom of my heart, that won\u2019t be true. It\u2019ll be because you\u2019re an a**hole.\"","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-7f30-8bed-6461852850ae","description":"\"I know who I am. I\u2019m the dude playing a dude disguised as another dude!\"","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-7211-8025-8c7b48248542","description":"\"Plastics.\"","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-7250-b7d3-c45329283d18","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-796c-8b3c-aa437bd658ff","question":"In what 1941 movie is the mysterious last word \'Rosebud\' whispered by the main character before his death?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"In Citizen Kane, Rosebud is revealed to be the name of Kane\u2019s childhood sled, symbolizing the happiness he lost.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-79c8-86f6-0116612a26af","description":"Citizen Kane","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-7744-aa74-1b16fa0f7bd2","description":"Casablanca","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-795b-b6eb-4ae5d189e8f5","description":"Gone with the Wind","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca-7a92-9a49-61b264b4c6d1","description":"The Maltese Falcon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-54ca